[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: sshswitch
diagnosis_text:
- Affected component: VLAN 5 forwarding on sshswitch (the trunk subinterfaces that carry VLAN 5).
- Mechanism: Campus 2 hosts in VLAN 5 can reach each other locally on switch4, but ARP to the default gateway 10.5.0.254 fails (pc1 shows “10.5.0.254 FAILED”), so off-subnet traffic dies. The physical uplink between switch4 and sshswitch is up, but VLAN 5 is not being forwarded across sshswitch, isolating the VLAN from the upstream L3 gateway.
- Localization: The physical trunk link ms1_sw4 (switch4.eth0 <-> sshswitch.eth0) is healthy at both ends (10G, LOWER_UP). On switch4, eth0.5 is in br_vlan5 and forwarding. On sshswitch, however, both eth0.5 (to switch4) and bond0.5 (to router17) are members of br_v5 but are in “state disabled” (bridge link show), preventing VLAN 5 frames from traversing the uplink.
- Root cause: VLAN 5 was administratively disabled on sshswitch (bridge ports eth0.5 and bond0.5 in br_v5 are disabled), not a physical trunk failure.
- Corrective fix: No recabling is required. Re-enable VLAN 5 on sshswitch by bringing br_v5 and its member ports eth0.5 and bond0.5 into forwarding state (restore VLAN 5 to the trunk/bond). Then verify the upstream L3 SVI for 10.5.0.254 is present/up on the router side. After re-enabling, ARP to 10.5.0.254 from pc1 should succeed and off-subnet connectivity should be restored.

=== END ===